From: WFI-030 — traceability matrix delivery-status normalization
Subject: [PATCH] feat(quality-loop): accept a status-normalized traceability digest at stage task

Human-applied patch. Both files are protected gate scripts, so an agent may
stage this diff but may not apply it. See docs/workflow-improvements/WFI-030.md.

Apply with:
    git apply reports/notes/wfi-030-traceability-status-normalization.patch

Scope: the first row of WFI-030's Proposed Change table only. The precheck-side
`frozen_artifact_done_when` detection and the reviewer-side adjudication
requirement (rows two and three) are NOT in this patch; they add a field to
precheck-result.json which tests/task-layer-review-inputs.tests.{sh,ps1}
consume, and that consumer has not been surveyed yet.

Validation already performed against the live corpus (WFI-030 Proposed Change):
  - normalization is a byte no-op on 31 of 34 specs/*/traceability.md; the 3
    that move are the profile: legacy features the freeze does not reach
  - Case B' (Planned -> Done) normalizes back to the recorded digest: accepted
  - Case A (Evidence-cell rewrite): rejected
  - Case B (Planned -> Delivered, out of vocabulary): rejected

Not yet performed: the fixture and twin-parity tests of WFI-030's Verification
Plan items 1-4. Do not treat this patch as verified until those run.

--- a/plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/check-workflow-state.sh
+++ b/plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/check-workflow-state.sh
@@ -252,6 +252,32 @@
   fi
   return 1
 }
+# The traceability matrix is the only task-stage input besides the task plan
+# that carries a field the workflow is designed to advance: each requirement
+# row's final cell records that requirement's delivery status. Binding the
+# whole file froze that column too -- no full-profile feature has ever moved a
+# row off the authoring-time default. This rewrites ONLY that one cell, and
+# only when it already holds a value from the closed lifecycle vocabulary the
+# state registry pins, so every other byte of every row -- code targets, test
+# IDs, evidence paths -- still participates in the digest, and a body edit
+# matches neither form. An out-of-vocabulary value is a body edit, not a
+# lifecycle transition, and stays bound.
+# The recorded digest is taken at authoring time, when every cell already holds
+# the default, so the recorded raw digest and this normalized digest coincide
+# there; that is why no producing-side field is needed.
+# The trailing [[:space:]]* absorbs a CR, so CRLF input round-trips without a
+# literal \r escape (BSD sed has none).
+traceability_normalized_hash() {
+  local file="$1"
+  LC_ALL=C sed -E \
+    -e 's/^(\|[[:space:]]*REQ-.*\|)([[:space:]]*)(Planned|In Progress|Implementation Complete|Done|Blocked)([[:space:]]*\|[[:space:]]*)$/\1\2Planned\4/' \
+    "$file" | sha256_stream
+}
+traceability_hash_accepted() {
+  local candidate="$1" raw="$2" normalized="$3"
+  [[ -n "$candidate" ]] || return 1
+  [[ "$candidate" == "$raw" || "$candidate" == "$normalized" ]]
+}
 manifest_has_hash() {
   local contract="$1" suffix="$2" expected="$3" recorded_root="$4"
   jq -e --arg suffix "$suffix" --arg expected "$expected" \
